# Line-ending policy for binary assets.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is set on this checkout. Git's text heuristic misclassifies
# small PDFs as text (they contain no NUL byte early enough), so it rewrites LF
# to CRLF on checkout — which silently changes the bytes of every PDF, including
# the ones under public/resources/ and public/press/. Declaring them binary
# stops any conversion in either direction.
*.pdf   binary

# Other binary asset types, for the same reason.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
